Main responsibilities
In this position you will be promoting strategic humanitarian responses guided by a critical understanding of MSF’s positioning within the given context. Developing and supporting operations with implementing the witnessing, protection and advocacy components of MSF’s work is what you will be working on. Along the way you will come across key humanitarian challenges that MSF is facing:
The levels of need for medical humanitarian assistance remain vast in many regions of the world, yet it is increasingly challenging to fulfil MSF’s social mission. Syria, Yemen, Afghanistan, South Sudan, Myanmar, and the Central African Republic are a few of the places where violence, abuse and neglect lead to human crises. Entire populations are threatened by outbreaks of disease, responses to which continue to be inadequate.
Factors such as global pandemics, urbanization and global migration may bring new types of health needs. At the same time, humanitarian responses must navigate an ever-shifting political landscape. Increasing restrictions to operations set by host states, instrumentalization, criminalisation and delegitimization of humanitarian action and the communities it seeks to support; and the politicisation, militarisation, privatisation and nationalisation of humanitarian assistance all affect the way humanitarian agencies operate and impact on their ability to respond.
Responsibilities and activities
Direct country support
Support, coaching and functional (technical) management of Humanitarian Affairs staff in country, supporting and orienting their work;
Providing country operations with political and contextual analysis on factors shaping the humanitarian landscape and issues MSF wants to leverage or influence;
Working with operational teams in identifying and documenting protection issues affecting the populations we serve, and defining MSF’s strategies to address them;
Driving consistent implementation of advocacy strategies;
Acting as a ‘sparring partner’ to the Heads of Mission and Operational Managers on protection issues, humanitarian principles and organizational positioning;
Advising country teams on the process of the gathering, analysis and synthesis of information/data;
Drafting of position papers, briefing documents, and public reports.
Thematic work
Identifying and developing key humanitarian themes for MSF, conducting research, writing papers, organising internal and external discussions;
Sharing MSF thinking and analysis through attending debates, workshops and conferences, writing articles and making presentations;
Developing and maintaining relevant networks, bringing cutting edge thinking into the organisation.
Training
The Humanitarian Affairs Advisor is also responsible for developing and delivering training modules for country teams and headquarters staff on humanitarian affairs, aimed at strengthening MSF’s humanitarian work.
Candidate Profile
We are looking for someone with:
Substantial experience (7+ years) in the field of humanitarian action, protection or human rights; at least 3-5 years in country experience in the types of contexts where MSF is active
Extensive knowledge and understanding of recent developments in the field of humanitarian action, migration, protection and international relations;
Academic background in areas relevant to MSF’s work, such as international relations, international human rights & humanitarian law and social sciences;
Strong analytical and advisory skills and the ability to translate complex analysis into concise, clear, and actionable conclusions and recommendations;
Proven excellence in written English and a track record writing reports, position papers or briefing notes; excellence in written French an advantage.
Excellent verbal communication and training skills;
Fluency in English required; and fluency or working knowledge of French is a strong advantage; working knowledge of Arabic is an advantage;
Regional expertise and/or understanding of geo-political factors influencing contexts where MSF is operational will be considered assets, as will an understanding of public health issues.

We are seeking a highly skilled and experienced candidate to join our team in the department of Design Monitoring Evaluation Accountability Learning (DMEAL) as Head of Design Quality and Impact reporting to Chief Operations Officer.
Overview
The Head of Design Quality and Impact will lead the Design, Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability and Leaming (DMEAL) team to guide in the effective conceptualization, development, implementation, and measurement of innovative, impactful, and sustainable community development programmes, aligned with The Maa Trust mission, vision, values, and strategic priorities. The incumbent will collaborate with the internal teams, partners, and stakeholders to design programmes that address key community challenges in the Maasai Mara landscape, secure funding, manage and assure quality of programme implementation, and achieve evidence-based outcomes and impact. The incumbent will further establish relevant policies, standards, and business processes to ensure an effective and efficient design, monitoring, evaluation, accountability and leaming function. The position will be based at The Maa Trust's HQ in the Maasai Mara, Narok County.
Roles and Responsibilities
Programme Design & Development
Take lead in conducting robust research, needs assessments, and situational analyses to identify target issues and beneficiaries in the Maasai Mara landscape
Apply expert knowledge, skills, experience and relevant tools and methodologies, in determining root-causes, articulating pathways to change, and establishing the theory of change (ToC) for development programmes and projects at The Mas Trust;
In collaboration with the programmes team, and, where necessary, other external stakeholders, conceptualize and co-create sustainable solutions that address the root-causes of the identified critical challenges among the community.
Ensure effective and seamless translation of strategy into programmes and from programmes into projects, as well as aligning donor funded project proposals to the programme designs:
Develop clear programme results frameworks, including goals, outcomes, outputs, activities, budgets, and monitoring and evaluation indicators;
Work with the field teams, technical experts, and partners to ensure programme relevance and feasibility: Contribute to the development of concept notes, proposals, and project plans for donors and stakeholders.
Quality Assurance and Accountability
Ensure effective development and deployment of strategy and programme implementation procedures as well as operational guidelines, in fulfilling strategic priorities and programme goals:
Ensure continued alignment of all programmes and projects to The Maa Trust strategic pillars and or priorities;
Ensure the mainstreaming of critical cross-cutting themes including child protection and adult safeguarding. gender mainstreaming, and link to conservation, among others;
Develop and deploy policies, standard operating procedures (SOPs) and business processes to monitor programme and project implementation to ensure adherence to donor and regulatory requirements, as well as meeting any specified sectoral/technical standards
Supporting conservation through sustainable community development in the Maasai Mara
Regularly conduct benchmarking studies and analysis with other development partners to draw lessons for continuous improvement of quality in programme and project management processes:
Continually provide evidence to assure stakeholders that programme and project results (outputs, outcomes, and impact) meet expectations and are up to desired quality standards, while strongly demonstrating causal linkage to key programme interventions;
Identify capacity development needs among programme teams and organize relevant training in programme. project management and MEL to ensure sustained quality standards.
Monitoring, Evaluation, and Learning
Lead the MEL team in developing the results framework, articulating impact, outcomes, outputs and relevant indicators with their baselines and target measures:
Lead and oversee development of robust MEL systems to track programme performance and achievement of set outcomes and goals and areas for improvement;
Lead in preparation of technical reports and content for impact reports to be disseminated to stakeholders, highlighting achievements;
Incorporate quality reporting mechanisms such as peer review, benchmarking, and continuous capacity building to ensure sustained quality reporting standards;
Organize and conduct reflection and learning forums for programme team, and identifying key improvement areas and adaptive management interventions;
Ensure evidence-based decision-making by integrating data and lessons learned into subsequent programme design and operations:
Develop departmental risk register, ensure its implementation to mitigate risks and ensure accountability. D. Collaboration and Stakeholder Engagement
Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders in ensuring effective planning and implementation of DMEAL function's goals and plans;
Ensure successful engagement of DMEAL team with the relevant external stakeholders, including community, local leaders, county and national government departments, research entities, among others in fulfilment of the function's mandate:
Coordinate the DMEAL team in supporting other departments such as communication, resource development, and finance in providing relevant information and data required for various reporting purposes;
Ensure preparation and presentation to the Board of Trustees of quarterly impact reports highlighting progress in programme implementation, achievements, challenges, risks and mitigations, and applied adaptive management mechanisms for continued effectiveness in implementation.
Team Management
Clearly communicates the organisation's strategy, goals and objectives to the DMEAL team, in development of clear departmental goals and plans;
Lead and manage the DMEAL team, to deliver on set goals providing guidance, support, and mentorship to team members:
Conduct regular performance appraisals and ensures the team is on track to fulfilling the department's expectations effectively and efficiently.
Lead and provide mentorship and coaching to ensures that the DMEAL team upholds quality standards in data collection, analysis, and reporting.
Supporting conservation through sustainable community development in the Maasai Mara
Foster a collaborative and inspiring work environment that encourage creativity, innovation, and professional growth;
Allocate resources effectively to meet communication objectives and ensures the team operates efficiently. Identify training needs and opportunities for team members to enhance their skills and capabilities. Organizes workshops, seminars, and training sessions to improve DMEAL skills and knowledge:
Encourages continuous learning and professional development to keep the team updated with industry trends.
QUALITICATIONS
Education and Experience
The incumbent should possess a Master's degree in Monitoring and Evaluation, Development Studies, or any of the fields of Social Sciences, Programme/Project Management, or Strategic Management;
Professional certification in programme/project management standards, and where possible certification specifically for humanitarian and development NGOs:
At least 5 years of progressive experience in programme management, with a focus on programme design, quality assurance and impact measurement in a development NGO or similar organization:
Demonstrated success in leading diverse teams and managing multi-sector programmes;
Strong experience with donor reporting and compliance (e.g. USAID, EU, UN agencies, DFID among others).
Skills
Exceptional leadership and strategic thinking and planning abilities;
Advanced knowledge and skills in programme design, monitoring, evaluation, and learning methodologies, including measurement and analysis of both quantitative and qualitative variables;
Strong project management skills;
Excellent communication, negotiation, and presentation skills;
Proficiency in programme management tools, research methods, data analysis software, and donor platforms

Main Clinical Duties And Responsibilities
Overseeing and monitoring Root Cause Analysis and Corrective Actions & Preventive Actions on all the audit findings and reporting the findings to the quality committee and recommending action plans and corrective measures promptly;
Ensure the culture of patient safety in all patient care areas which includes deliverance of safe clinical practices, identification of patient & avoidance of medication errors;
Attending medical-legal cases pertaining to the Hospital, in coordination with the Lead Consultant, Management and CEO;
Coordinate and supervise the attendance of Medical Officers, consultants/visiting consultants and ensure they comply with the set protocols. Facilitate orientation of the clinical staff;
Has overall responsibility for delivery of quality primary and secondary health care. This includes ensuring clinical practices that guarantee high-quality clinical outcomes; providing supervision and advice on clinical activities, including both outpatient and inpatient services, ward rounds, and surgical interventions; promoting a culture of learning and keeping up up-to-date on diagnostic and treatment practices;
Heading the medical records department and make sure that all the records are properly archived as per hospital policy, closed audits of case sheets are being done by Medical Records team, proper file coding is being followed and any record should not be given to patient/attendant/consultant/legal authorities without the permission or sign off of the Medical Superintendent and the Lead Consultant;
Ensures that clinical cases that require treatment beyond the hospital’s capacity are referred to a higher service in a timely and professional manner. Develop networks with referral hospitals to facilitate referral processes;
Develops and implements strategies to ensure that staff comply with quality assurance guidelines; monitors service quality and for investigating incidents and complaints in the hospital;
Together with clinical heads of department, provides leadership in the formulation, implementation, and review of and compliance with all internal standard operating procedures (SOPs) and treatment protocols; ensures adherence at all levels in the facility with set standards; oversees adherence to appropriate medical waste management and infection control practices and protocols;
Represents and manages the relationship and communication between the hospital and regulatory bodies;
Promotes the use and internal consumption of collected data within the facility to inform decisions impacting patient care, financial management, and clinical outcomes. Participates with the Management and other heads of departments in data analysis and interpretation;
Main Managerial Responsibilities
Ensures favorable staff working environment within approved budget and needs;
Supervises senior hospital management team activities, ensuring that patients and staff concerns and needs are attended to and that departments are managed proactively with a view to improving efficiency and maintaining professional etiquette;
Together with the lead consultant and medical officers, it organizes and facilitates capacity-building sessions through mentoring, coaching, in-service training, and continuing medical education (CME);
Leads, with the department heads, the personnel recruitment and selection process; periodical and annual appraisals; performance reviews and discipline. Ensures that all medical staff in contact with patients are licensed by their respective professional body; that the licenses are up to date and that a record of such license is kept in the staff personnel files;
Chairs meetings with hospital clinical staff and ensures appropriate and periodic CMEs and relevant training for staff;
Promotes and nurtures a culture of good stewardship, accountability, and transparency at all levels of hospital operations;
Facilitates the sustainability of hospital operations via the development of public/private partnerships, collaboration with private doctors and hospitals;
Reviewing the staffing rotas to ensure they are all well prepared taking into shift safety and business levels in addition to ensuring that they are accurate and submitted in a timely manner;
Any other duties asmay be assigned
Qualifications And Requirements Competencies And Skills
Deep passion for access to healthcare change;
Qualified medical doctor with surgical skills and at least 10 years’ clinical experience; valid medical registration license;
Previous clinical practice and/or experience working in a maternity hospital hospital(s);
Knowledge of computerized hospital management systems is an advantage;
Ability to understand data across many clients–looking for patterns in outcomes, care, etc;
Fluency in written – good presentation skills and spoken English;
Previous experience in hospital staff supervision, quality management, inter-departmental coordination, coaching, and training;
Previous experience in a similar medical superintendent position is an added advantage
